        <div class="about-project">
            <h2 class="about-project__title">Why Unity Architecture Exists</h2>

            <div class="about-project__body">
                <p>
                    Unity Architecture was created to solve a problem I encountered
                    repeatedly throughout my career — most Unity developers know how to
                    write code, but very few are taught how to design systems.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The goal is not simply to teach Unity. The goal is to teach
                    developers how to think like software architects. Architecture is
                    one of the least understood areas of Unity development, yet one of
                    the most valuable skills a developer can acquire.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The handbook teaches the principles. The toolkit demonstrates the
                    implementation. Together they provide both understanding and
                    practical experience — helping developers transition from writing
                    working code to designing maintainable software.
                </p>
                <p>
                    If a developer begins creating cleaner, more scalable Unity projects
                    because of this ecosystem, then the mission is achieved.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

